# NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-BF16

<div align="center" style="line-height: 1;">
--
## Description

**NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-BF16** is the full-precision release of NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Super VL, a vision-language model for reasoning, coding, tool use, document understanding, and video understanding. The BF16 weights support customization, domain adaptation, and full-precision evaluation. For optimized deployment, see the [NVFP4 release](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4).

The model combines interleaved Mamba-2, Mixture-of-Experts (MoE), and attention layers with a C-RADIO vision encoder and a vision-language connector. It has **120B total parameters** and **12B active parameters** and supports context lengths up to **1M tokens**. Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) enables native speculative decoding.

This model is ready for commercial or non-commercial use.
--
| | |
|:---|:---|
| **Total Parameters** | 120B (12B active) |
| **Architecture** | Mamba-2–Transformer hybrid Mixture of Experts with a C-RADIO vision encoder |
| **Precision** | BF16 (full-precision reference weights) |
| **Context Length** | Up to 1M tokens; deployment settings are listed below |
--
| **Deployment** | 4× H100 or 2× GB200 |
| **Speculative Decoding** | Native Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) |
| **Reasoning Mode** | Configurable through the chat template (`enable_thinking=True/False`) |
| **Recommended Sampling** | Text: temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95; vision: temperature 0.6, top_p 0.95 |
| **Best For** | Customization, domain adaptation, and full-precision evaluation |
--
## Quick Start

For efficient inference on DGX Spark or data center GPUs, see the [NVFP4 card](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4). The example below serves BF16 on **4× H100**.

Nemotron 3.5 Super VL has configurable reasoning levels: off, on (medium), and on. Selecting on (medium) will reduce the number of tokens generated compared to on, but may impact accuracy. You can learn about the reasoning budget [here](https://huggingface.co/nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-BF16#text-and-reasoning)!

Use Docker with NVIDIA GPU support and the `vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-3f1bcfd82bb2e93fcd364fc7a5491718453a77e2` or (`vllm/vllm-openai:v0.32.0`) image. If the model requires authentication, set `HF_TOKEN` in your shell before launching the container.

```bash
export MODEL=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-BF16
```

